{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "FireFluxToAtmosphereWRFFire",
  "description": "Fire -> atmosphere feedback of NCAR fire_behavior within WRF (io/wrf_mod.F90: Provide_atm_feedback and Fire_tendency). (1) Aggregation: the sensible and latent heat fluxes of the sr_x x sr_y fire cells under an atmosphere cell are averaged, grnhfx = mean_s fgrnhfx_s (W/m^2); the canopy fluxes canhfx/canqfx are inputs (0 in fire_behavior, which has no crown fire). (2) Vertical distribution: the surface flux decays exponentially with height above ground with the extinction depth alfg (fire_ext_grnd), the canopy flux is constant up to z1can (fire_crwn_hgt) and decays with alfc above it; the kinematic fluxes on the w-levels are F_h(z) = f grnhfx e^(-z/alfg)/cp + canhfx c(z)/cp and F_q(z) = f grnqfx e^(-z/alfg)/xlv + canqfx c(z)/xlv with f = fire_atm_feedback. (3) The layer tendencies are the flux divergence, written as the PDE dtheta/dt = -(1/rho) dF_h/dz and lowered on the column_nonuniform_1d grid (ze = WRF z_at_w) by the face-flux rule, which reproduces WRF's (F_{k+1} - F_k)/dz8w_k exactly; WRF stores them mass-weighted, rthfrten = (c1h mu + c2h) dtheta/dt (Pa K/s; the hybrid-coordinate column mass factor replaces calculate_phy_tend), and leaves the top layer at 0 (its loop stops at kde - 2): rthfrten_wrf makes that truncation explicit, rthfrten itself carries the flux of the extrapolated top face. Note WRF divides the heat flux by cp and calls the result a theta tendency (theta ~ T, no Exner factor), transcribed as written. Compared with WRF-SFIRE's fire_tendency (phys/module_fr_fire_atm.F, ifire = 2): the aggregation is identical (test7/wrf.nc GRNHFX reproduced to 0), but SFIRE multiplies the profile by a prop_heat(i,k,j) factor, so its RTHFRTEN differs from this component by 0.7-1.5 % in test7/wrf.nc. Tests: fire_behavior's Provide_atm_feedback replayed by the EarthSciML feedback driver (data/eqwefic/fire_build/feedback_driver, instrumented firelib 8d519c6, real32) on the atmosphere columns of test7/wrf.nc frames 5 and 10 (t = 5, 10 s) with (a) the fire-mesh fluxes stored in wrf.nc and (b) fire_behavior's own fluxes of the standalone test7 run at step 10 (the CFBM-consistent coupled chain); rel 1e-5.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wildland_fire",
   "fire_behavior",
   "wrf-fire",
   "coupling",
   "heat-flux"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580; instrumented fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior branch earthsciml-instrumented (8d519c6: coupling dumps). WRF v4.8.0 registry.fire defaults fire_ext_grnd = fire_ext_crwn = 50 m, fire_crwn_hgt = 15 m, fire_atm_feedback = 1."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 44,
   "description": "Number of atmosphere layers (WRF kte = kde - 1; 44 for the 45-level test7 column). Bound into the column grid at the import edge."
  },
  "NSUB": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Number of fire cells under one atmosphere cell, sr_x * sr_y (test7: 4 x 4)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "subcell": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NSUB"
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "FireFluxToAtmosphereWRFFire": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "wrf": {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "fgrnhfx_block": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "subcell"
     ],
     "description": "Sensible heat flux of the fire cells under the atmosphere cell (fire_behavior fgrnhfx = FireHeatFlux phi_h per fire cell, Fortran order over the sr_x x sr_y block). Consumer-supplied: a coupling target in a mounting document, a `parameter_overrides` array in a test."
    },
    "fgrnqfx_block": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "subcell"
     ],
     "description": "Latent heat flux of the fire cells (fgrnqfx = FireHeatFlux phi_q). Consumer-supplied: a coupling target in a mounting document, a `parameter_overrides` array in a test."
    },
    "s_coupled": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Coupling hook: index (1-based) of the fire cell whose fluxes are taken from phi_h_in/phi_q_in instead of the block (0 = none). Lets a coupled document drive one fire cell's flux from a FireHeatFlux model."
    },
    "phi_h_in": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Coupling target: sensible heat flux of fire cell s_coupled (variable_map from FireHeatFlux.phi_h)."
    },
    "phi_q_in": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Coupling target: latent heat flux of fire cell s_coupled (variable_map from FireHeatFlux.phi_q)."
    },
    "fgrnhfx_eff": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "subcell"
     ],
     "description": "Block fluxes with cell s_coupled replaced by phi_h_in."
    },
    "fgrnqfx_eff": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "subcell"
     ],
     "description": "Block fluxes with cell s_coupled replaced by phi_q_in."
    },
    "canhfx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Canopy (crown fire) sensible heat flux on the atmosphere cell; 0 in fire_behavior."
    },
    "canqfx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Canopy latent heat flux; 0 in fire_behavior."
    },
    "mu": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "Pa",
     "default": 80000.0,
     "description": "Dry air mass of the column (WRF mut = mu + mub)."
    },
    "alfg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 50.0,
     "description": "Extinction depth of the surface fire heat (fire_ext_grnd)."
    },
    "alfc": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 50.0,
     "description": "Extinction depth of the crown fire heat above z1can (fire_ext_crwn)."
    },
    "z1can": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 15.0,
     "description": "Height of the crown fire heat release (fire_crwn_hgt)."
    },
    "fire_atm_feedback": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Multiplier of the surface fluxes fed back to the atmosphere (fire_atm_feedback; 0 switches the feedback off, in which case WRF returns zero tendencies)."
    },
    "ze": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Height of the w-levels (WRF z_at_w, above sea level), the grid's geometry input. Consumer-supplied: a coupling target in a mounting document, a `parameter_overrides` array in a test."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer thickness ze[k+1] - ze[k] (WRF dz8w), from the grid template."
    },
    "rho": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer air density (WRF rho). Consumer-supplied: a coupling target in a mounting document, a `parameter_overrides` array in a test."
    },
    "c1h": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Hybrid-coordinate weight c1h of the mass levels. Consumer-supplied: a coupling target in a mounting document, a `parameter_overrides` array in a test."
    },
    "c2h": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Hybrid-coordinate weight c2h of the mass levels. Consumer-supplied: a coupling target in a mounting document, a `parameter_overrides` array in a test."
    },
    "avgw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1/(sr_x sr_y), the averaging weight of the fire cells."
    },
    "grnhfx": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Surface sensible heat flux on the atmosphere cell: mean of the fire-cell fluxes (Provide_atm_feedback grnhfx)."
    },
    "grnqfx": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Surface latent heat flux on the atmosphere cell (grnqfx)."
    },
    "z_w": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Height of the w-levels above ground, ze - ze[1]."
    },
    "decay_g": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Surface-fire decay e^(-z_w/alfg)."
    },
    "decay_c": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Crown-fire profile: 1 below z1can, e^(-(z_w - z1can)/alfc) above."
    },
    "F_h": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K*kg/m^2/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Kinematic sensible heat flux on the w-levels (Fire_tendency hfx): (fire_atm_feedback grnhfx decay_g + canhfx decay_c)/cp."
    },
    "F_q": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Kinematic moisture flux on the w-levels (Fire_tendency qfx): (fire_atm_feedback grnqfx decay_g + canqfx decay_c)/xlv."
    },
    "dtheta_dt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Potential-temperature tendency -(1/rho) dF_h/dz of each layer (the physics; layer NLEV uses the extrapolated top face)."
    },
    "dqv_dt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Water-vapour tendency -(1/rho) dF_q/dz."
    },
    "mass_factor": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "c1h mu + c2h, the hybrid-coordinate column mass WRF multiplies the tendencies by."
    },
    "rthfrten": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa*K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Mass-weighted theta tendency as WRF stores it, (c1h mu + c2h) dtheta_dt."
    },
    "rqvfrten": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Mass-weighted qv tendency, (c1h mu + c2h) dqv_dt."
    },
    "rthfrten_wrf": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa*K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "rthfrten with the top layer set to 0, as WRF's Fire_tendency leaves it (loop k = kts .. kde - 2)."
    },
    "rqvfrten_wrf": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "rqvfrten with the top layer set to 0 (WRF truncation)."
    }
   },
